  "id": "functional-level",
  "term": "functional level",
  "definition": "In this historical source, functional level means a relative grade of nervous or cerebral activity, ranging from higher to lower forms of operation. A disturbance at a lower functional level is described as affecting more elementary functions and as being more open to control by outside stimuli or suggestion.",
